bottled-lila
NOTICE

WHAT THIS REPOSITORY IS
=======================

This repository is packaging: it builds a container image that runs the
Lichess server (lila) as a Cloud in a Bottle app. It does not contain the
chess server itself. The image is built on top of upstream Lichess
container images and adds an app manifest, a Dockerfile, process
supervision configuration, an internal reverse-proxy configuration, a
first-boot init script, and an authentication proxy.

The resulting image redistributes software licensed under the GNU Affero
General Public License version 3, so the image as a whole is distributed
under AGPL-3.0. A verbatim copy of that license is in the LICENSE file
beside this one. The packaging files written for this repository are
additionally offered under the MIT License (full text at the end of this
file); that extra grant does not remove the AGPL-3.0 obligations that
attach to the image.


UPSTREAM COMPONENTS
===================

lila (the Lichess chess server)
  https://github.com/lichess-org/lila
  AGPL-3.0-or-later
  Copyright (c) 2012-2026 the lila authors
  lila's COPYING.md states AGPL version 3 or later, with exceptions for
  bundled media assets. See the ASSET LICENSING CAVEAT below, which
  matters for anyone using this image commercially.

lila-ws (the Lichess WebSocket server)
  https://github.com/lichess-org/lila-ws
  AGPL-3.0

lila-docker
  https://github.com/lichess-org/lila-docker
  AGPL-3.0
  Provides the base image this repository extends,
  ghcr.io/lichess-org/lila-docker:latest, which is the single-container
  ("mono") image from that project. It ships pre-built lila and lila-ws
  along with MongoDB, Redis and Caddy.

lila-fishnet (the AI move broker)
  https://github.com/lichess-org/lila-fishnet
  AGPL-3.0
  Consumed as the pre-built image ghcr.io/lichess-org/lila-fishnet:3.0.18.
  The application and the JDK it ships with are copied into this image.

fishnet (the Stockfish worker)
  https://github.com/lichess-org/fishnet
  GPL-3.0-or-later
  Pinned release v2.8.1. The upstream static Linux x86_64 binary is
  downloaded at image build time. That binary carries the chess engines
  fishnet runs: Stockfish (https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish)
  and, for chess variants, Fairy-Stockfish
  (https://github.com/ianfab/Fairy-Stockfish). Both engines are
  GPL-3.0-or-later. Run "fishnet license" for the license text the binary
  itself ships.

lila-db-seed
  https://github.com/lichess-org/lila-db-seed
  MIT
  Sample database fixtures (users, tournaments, openings). Baked into the
  upstream base image and copied into the app's data directory on first
  boot, so this image redistributes them.

MongoDB, Redis and Caddy are bundled by the upstream base image
(ghcr.io/lichess-org/lila-docker:latest) rather than installed by this
repository. They keep their own licenses: Caddy is Apache-2.0, MongoDB
Community builds are under the Server Side Public License, and Redis is
BSD-3-Clause through release 7.2 and dual RSALv2 / SSPLv1 from 7.4 onward.
Inspect the base image to see which versions, and therefore which of those
terms, apply to a given build.


SOURCE OFFER (AGPL-3.0 SECTION 13, GPL-3.0 SECTION 6)
=====================================================

Complete Corresponding Source for every component listed above is publicly
available from the upstream repositories at the URLs listed above. The
Corresponding Source for the packaging in this image is this repository
itself.

The exact pinned artifacts a build of this image uses:

  base image (lila, lila-ws, MongoDB, Redis, Caddy):
      ghcr.io/lichess-org/lila-docker:latest
      source: https://github.com/lichess-org/lila-docker
              https://github.com/lichess-org/lila
              https://github.com/lichess-org/lila-ws

  AI move broker:
      ghcr.io/lichess-org/lila-fishnet:3.0.18
      source: https://github.com/lichess-org/lila-fishnet

  Stockfish worker:
      fishnet v2.8.1
      source: https://github.com/lichess-org/fishnet
      release: https://github.com/lichess-org/fishnet/releases/tag/v2.8.1

  packaging:
      this repository

Important: the base image is pinned only by the mutable tag ":latest", so
the tag alone does not identify one revision of lila or lila-ws. Record the
resolved image digest at build time (for example with "docker buildx
imagetools inspect ghcr.io/lichess-org/lila-docker:latest", or "docker
image inspect" on the pulled image) and keep that digest with the built
image. The digest is what lets the exact upstream source revision behind a
given build be identified later. Whoever distributes a build of this image,
or offers network access to it, is responsible for providing Corresponding
Source that matches the digest they used.

Requests for the Corresponding Source used by a build published from this
repository can be sent to andrew@laack.co, or filed as an issue on this
repository.


ASSET LICENSING CAVEAT (READ BEFORE ANY COMMERCIAL USE)
=======================================================

lila's COPYING.md lists exceptions to the AGPL for bundled media, and some of
those exceptions forbid commercial use.

Many of the piece sets under public/piece/ are licensed
CC BY-NC-SA (Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike), which
permits non-commercial use only: at the time of writing that covers
anarcandy, caliente, california, cardinal, cooke, disguised, dubrovny,
fresca, gioco, horsey, icpieces, maestro, monarchy, staunty, tatiana and
xkcd. The sound set public/sounds/lisp is CC BY-NC-SA as well. lila's
"Exceptions (non-free)" table restricts further assets: public/piece/alpha is
"free for personal non commercial use", several piece sets are labelled only
"freeware", some carry no stated license at all, the Lichess logo and favicon
may be used only to refer to lichess.org, and the remaining sounds under
public/sound and artwork under public/images are covered by that same
non-free list.

The upstream base image ships lila's public/ directory wholesale, so this
image contains those assets.

Consequence, stated plainly: this image, as built, may not be used or
redistributed commercially. Anyone who wants to redistribute or operate it
commercially must first strip out or replace every asset that is restricted
to non-commercial or personal use, or obtain separate permission from the
asset authors. Check the current per-asset tables in lila's COPYING.md
(https://github.com/lichess-org/lila/blob/master/COPYING.md) before relying
on any of this, because the set of bundled assets changes upstream.


